      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n`GaugeManager.notifyRewardAmount` unconditionally pulls the epoch emission from the minter, but it only updates the distribution index when there is non-zero voting weight:\n\n```solidity\n\nuint256 _ratio = 0;\nuint256 totalWeight = IVoter(voter).totalWeight();\nif (totalWeight > 0) _ratio = amount * 1e18 / Math.max(totalWeight, 1);\nif (_ratio > 0) {\n    index += _ratio;\n}\n```\n\nWhen every voter has reset (`totalWeight == 0`), the transfer `HYBR::transferFrom(minter, GaugeManager, amount)` still executes, yet `index` remains unchanged. Later, `_updateForAfterDistribution` calculates each gauge’s share from `index - supplyIndex[gauge]`. Because that delta is zero, `claimable[gauge]` never increases, and the freshly minted HYBR is effectively orphaned inside `GaugeManager`.\n\nThe failure follows the normal epoch maintenance playbook:\n1. Voters call `reset` in the next epoch’s window to reclaim bribes, bringing `totalWeight` to zero.\n2. A keeper (or the minter itself) calls `distributeAll()`, which mints and transfers the weekly emission into `GaugeManager`.\n3. Because `index` is unchanged, all gauges remain at `claimable == 0`, and the HYBR balance becomes unrecoverable.\n\nThe PoC shows that with current parameters the first weekly emission mints ~2.47M HYBR into `GaugeManager`, leaves `claimable[gauge]` at zero, and later distributions do not touch the stranded balance. There is no refund or recovery mechanism, so every occurrence permanently removes an entire emission cycle from the reward flow. This is a protocol-level loss affecting all liquidity providers and voters, so the severity is **High**.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nBefore transferring rewards, ensure `totalWeight > 0`. Either:\n- skip the transfer and keep HYBR on the minter until weight is positive, or  \n- immediately return the funds to the minter and log the missed emission, or  \n- store the amount in a dedicated rollover accumulator that is added to the next positive-weight distribution.\n- Add operator tooling/alerts so that if an emission is skipped (zero weight), governance can decide whether to re-run once voting power returns.",
      "proofOfConcept": "1. Install dependencies inside `ve33/` (`npm install`), then run:\n   ```bash\n\n   cd ve33\n   forge test --match-test submissionValidity -vvv\n   ```\n   \n2. The PoC (`ve33/test/C4PoC.t.sol`) deploys the full stack (no mocks), creates a HYBR/gHYBR gauge, votes once, resets to make `totalWeight == 0`, and calls `GaugeManager.distributeAll()`. HYBR is minted and transferred to `GaugeManager` while all gauges keep `claimable == 0`.  \n3. After re-voting and distributing again, new rewards reach the gauge, yet the earlier emission remains in `GaugeManager`, demonstrating the permanent loss.\n\n```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport {HybraTimeLibrary} from \"../contracts/libraries/HybraTimeLibrary.sol\";\n\n/**\n * PoC: Emissions get stuck when weekly mint occurs with totalWeight == 0.\n * - Uses ONLY the real stack via C4PoCTestbed (no mocked contract-initiated calls).\n * - Ensures veNFT has voting power across epochs (avoids ZV).\n * - Pair creation uses try/catch; whitelists tokens only if required.\n */\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    address internal pool;\n    address internal gauge;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        bribeFactoryV3.initialize(\n            address(voter),\n            address(gaugeManager),\n            address(permissionsRegistry),\n            address(tokenHandler)\n        );\n\n        // Ensure we hold the role needed for whitelisting.\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GOVERNANCE\");\n\n        // Whitelist HYBR and gHYBR and mark HYBR as connector so gauge creation passes access checks.\n        address[] memory tokensToWhitelist = new address[](2);\n        tokensToWhitelist[0] = address(hybr);\n        tokensToWhitelist[1] = address(gHybr);\n        tokenHandler.whitelistTokens(tokensToWhitelist);\n        tokenHa